The circuit applies a constant \(V_{DS}=1\,\text{V}\) to NMOS transistor \(M_1\) while \(V_{GS}=V_X\) is swept. Consequently \(I_X=I_D\) follows the standard MOSFET transfer characteristic:

- \(I_X=0\) for \(V_X\le V_{TH}\) (cutoff);
- \(I_X=\frac12\mu_nC_{ox}(W/L)(V_X-V_{TH})^2\) for \(V_{TH}<V_X<V_{TH}+1\) (saturation);
- \(I_X=\mu_nC_{ox}(W/L)\bigl[(V_X-V_{TH})-\frac12\bigr]\) for \(V_X>V_{TH}+1\) (triode).

The two pieces meet with continuous value and slope at the saturation/triode boundary, so the plot is a parabola that becomes a straight line of slope \(\mu_nC_{ox}(W/L)\).

Final answer: \(I_X=0\) (\(V_X\le V_{TH}\)); sat. parabola then triode line
